meta {
  name: Update Activity
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/activities/1
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "booked",
    "confirmation_number": "MEIJI2025010301",
    "booking_url": "https://example.com/booking/MEIJI2025010301",
    "notes": "Confirmed booking for guided tour. Meet at main entrance at 09:00."
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Activity

  Updates an existing activity. All fields are optional - only send fields you want to change.

  ## URL Parameters
  - `activity_id`: The ID of the activity to update

  ## Updatable Fields
  All fields from ActivityUpdate schema are optional:
  - `name`: Activity name
  - `activity_type`: Type enum
  - `time`: Start time (HH:MM format)
  - `duration`: Duration in hours (decimal)
  - `location`: Location name
  - `location_address`: Full address
  - `latitude`: GPS latitude
  - `longitude`: GPS longitude
  - `cost`: Cost amount
  - `currency`: ISO currency code
  - `booking_required`: Boolean
  - `confirmation_number`: Booking confirmation
  - `booking_url`: URL to booking
  - `contact_phone`: Contact phone
  - `contact_email`: Contact email
  - `status`: Status enum (planned, booked, completed, cancelled)
  - `notes`: Additional notes

  ## Common Use Cases

  **Mark as booked:**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "booked",
    "confirmation_number": "ABC123"
  }
  ```

  **Update time:**
  ```json
  {
    "time": "10:30",
    "notes": "Time changed from 09:00 to 10:30"
  }
  ```

  **Mark as completed:**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "completed",
    "notes": "Great experience! Highly recommend."
  }
  ```

  ## Access Control
  - Requires authentication
  - User must own the trip
  - Returns 403 if unauthorized
}
